# Session Plan: {Feature Name}

**Created:** YYYY-MM-DD
**Total sessions:** N
**LOC budget per session:** ~1200
**Branch:** {from tech-spec frontmatter `branch:`}

> **Branch discipline (fill per session, ALWAYS state it in the session prompt).**
> Every implementation session MUST declare which branch it works on — in large repos there
> are many branches and an unstated branch is a real footgun. Default rule:
> - Multi-session / multi-component feature, or the default branch is prod (dev=prod=origin=VPS):
>   work on an ISOLATED `feature/{name}` branch + git worktree (parallel-tracks). Branch off the
>   default branch (which holds the specs). Merge back to the default branch only in the FINAL
>   session after green QA, via the integration train (PR + CI).
> - Small, low-risk change on a non-prod default branch: the default branch is acceptable.
> Take the branch from the tech-spec frontmatter `branch:` field; do NOT leave it implicit.

